      "writtenOn": "2020-12-10T07:12:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure we\u0027ll be able to do this.  The long-term goal of the ZeroCopy{Reader,Write} traits is to avoid keeping a buffer by using the splice(2) syscall, which requires an fd. We could probably change the File requirement to a marker trait but we would still need an fd.\n\nIn the case where there is no fd, buffering like we\u0027re doing here would still be necessary but at least there would only be one copy.",
      "revId": "6ddab6e3ef4f5fc08b84b5344bbbee5f7e348841",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
